    difficulty:'Intermediate', order:5, isPublished:true,
    content:`## What is CSV?\n**Comma Separated Values** — plain text, each value separated by comma. Opens in Excel.\n\nExample CSV content:\n\`\`\`\nrollno,name,marks,city\n1,Rahul Sharma,85,Unchahar\n2,Priya Singh,92,Raebareli\n\`\`\`\n\n## csv Module Functions\n\n| Function | Use |\n|----------|-----|\n| csv.writer(file) | Create writer object |\n| writer.writerow(list) | Write ONE row |\n| writer.writerows(list_of_lists) | Write MULTIPLE rows at once |\n| csv.reader(file) | Create reader object |\n\n## Important Rule\nAlways use \`newline=""\` when opening CSV for writing — prevents extra blank lines between rows.`,
    syntax:`import csv\n\n# Writing CSV\nwith open("students.csv", "w", newline="") as f:\n    writer = csv.writer(f)\n    writer.writerow(["rollno", "name", "marks", "city"])  # header\n    writer.writerow([1, "Rahul Sharma", 85, "Unchahar"])\n    writer.writerow([2, "Priya Singh",  92, "Raebareli"])\n\n# writerows — write multiple rows at once\nmore_data = [\n    [3, "Amit Kumar",  78, "Lucknow"],\n    [4, "Sneha Gupta", 88, "Allahabad"],\n]\nwith open("students.csv", "a", newline="") as f:\n    writer = csv.writer(f)\n    writer.writerows(more_data)\n\n# Reading CSV\nwith open("students.csv", "r") as f:\n    reader = csv.reader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        print(row)  # each row is a list: ['1','Rahul',…]\n\n# Skip header row when reading\nwith open("students.csv", "r") as f:\n    reader = csv.reader(f)\n    next(reader)  # skip header\n    for row in reader:\n        print("Name:", row[1], "Marks:", row[2])\n\n# Search userid/password program\ndef search_password(user_id):\n    with open("users.csv", "r") as f:\n        reader = csv.reader(f)\n        for row in reader:\n            if row[0] == user_id:\n                print("Password found:", row[1])\n                return\n    print("User ID not found!")`,
    keyPoints:['import csv required','newline="" in open() prevents extra blank lines','writerow() writes ONE row, writerows() writes MULTIPLE rows','reader() returns each row as a list of strings','next(reader) skips the header row','CSV is a text file — can be opened in Excel or Notepad'],
    tips:['Always newline="" when writing or you get extra blank rows','Use "a" mode to add data without deleting existing data','CSV values are always strings — use int() or float() to convert','Use next(reader) to skip header before processing data rows'],
    commonMistakes:['Forgetting newline="" — creates extra blank rows in output','Not importing csv module','CSV numbers are strings by default — must convert explicitly','Using "w" when you want to append — loses all existing data!'],
