    difficulty:'Basic', order:10, isPublished:true,
    content:`## What is a Computer Network?\nGroup of computers connected to **share data and resources**.\n\n## Evolution of Networking\n\n### ARPANET (1969)\n- First computer network\n- Created by US Department of Defense (DARPA)\n- Connected 4 universities initially\n- First use of **packet switching**\n- Full form: Advanced Research Projects Agency NETwork\n\n### NSFNET (1986)\n- National Science Foundation NETwork\n- Replaced ARPANET\n- Connected US universities and research centers\n- Speed: 56 Kbps → upgraded to 45 Mbps\n\n### INTERNET (1991 onwards)\n- Global network of networks\n- **Tim Berners-Lee** invented WWW (World Wide Web) in 1991\n- Open to the public\n- Uses TCP/IP protocols\n- Billions of devices connected today\n\n## 5 Components of Data Communication\n1. **Sender** — device that sends data\n2. **Receiver** — device that receives data\n3. **Message** — the data being sent\n4. **Communication Media** — path (cable or wireless)\n5. **Protocols** — rules for communication\n\n## Switching Techniques\n- **Circuit Switching** — dedicated path reserved for entire session (telephone calls)\n- **Packet Switching** — data split into packets, each can take different route (internet)`,
    syntax:`import socket\nhostname = socket.gethostname()\nip = socket.gethostbyname(hostname)\nprint("Hostname:", hostname)\nprint("IP Address:", ip)\n\n# Memory trick — evolution order:\n# ARPANET (1969) → NSFNET (1986) → INTERNET (1991)\n# Defense        → Science       → Public\n\n# Switching comparison:\n# Circuit Switching = dedicated path = telephone\n#   → whole path reserved, wastes if idle\n# Packet Switching  = data in packets = internet\n#   → efficient, packets take different routes`,
    keyPoints:['ARPANET (1969) — first network, US Defense, packet switching','NSFNET (1986) — academic/research, replaced ARPANET','Internet (1991) — public, Tim Berners-Lee invented WWW','5 components: Sender, Receiver, Message, Media, Protocols','Packet Switching = internet, Circuit Switching = telephone','IP address = unique address of every device on network'],
    tips:['Remember order: ARPANET → NSFNET → INTERNET and years 1969, 1986, 1991','Packet switching: data in packets, can take different routes, efficient','Tim Berners-Lee invented WWW, not the internet itself'],
    commonMistakes:['Confusing ARPANET year (1969) with NSFNET (1986)','Saying internet was invented by USA — WWW was by Tim Berners-Lee','Confusing Bandwidth (max capacity) with Speed (actual transfer rate)'],
