    keyPoints:['WWW created by Tim Berners-Lee in 1991 at CERN','HTML creates web pages; XML stores/transports data','URL = complete address: protocol + domain + path','Domain extensions: .com .edu .gov .in .org','Web hosting = renting server space to publish website','HTTPS = HTTP + SSL = secure, shows padlock in browser'],
    tips:['URL has 3 main parts: protocol + domain + path','WWW is a service ON the internet — not the internet itself','Tim Berners-Lee invented WWW, not the internet'],
    commonMistakes:['Saying WWW and internet are same thing — they are different','Confusing HTML (creates web pages) with HTTP (transfers web pages)','Forgetting domain extension meanings in exam'],
